{
  "title": "Keep a late meal-plan response from dismissing a reopened sheet",
  "description": "AddToMealPlanModal.tsx tracks and clears its 1500ms close timer, but handleAddToMealPlan does not check whether the modal was closed while createMealPlan was in flight. \
Pressing Escape during a pending submission and reopening lets the late response set mealPlanSuccess and arm closeTimer, so the reopened modal shows the success message and then closes itself. \
AddToMealPlanSheet.swift starts an unowned Task that does `try? await Task.sleep` and then sets the shared isPresented binding to false; the task is never cancelled on disappear and the `try?` swallows cancellation, so swiping the sheet away and reopening within a second dismisses the new presentation. \
AddToShoppingListModal.tsx (presentation counter) and SheetAutoDismissSupport.swift (cancellable dismiss task) show the fix for the shopping-list sheet; apply the same here and cover close/reopen during both pending submission and success on web and iOS.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
